    {
      "body": "The error is fixed and Q6 now runs: the container returns **0.77** (`conversion_probability` 0.769799), the same as Q4.\n\n**What was wrong:** the Q6 cell checks the container's model checksum against a variable called `expected`, but the cell that defined it had been deleted. That's why `hashlib` was imported but never used. My first attempt to add it back last time didn't take effect, so it was still missing.\n\n**What I changed:** I added two cells right after the setup cell:\n- A markdown cell: \"Check the artifact checksum before unpickling it.\"\n- A code cell that reads `model_sha256` from `model_metadata.json` into `expected` and checks it against the actual SHA256 of `pipeline.bin`. They match (`1646bbdc\u2026`).\n\nI then ran the checksum cell and both Q6 cells. The container reported the same model checksum and returned the same prediction as your local server in Q4. The cell's `finally` step stops the container afterwards, so nothing is left running.\n\nYour answers so far:\n\n| Q | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| Q1 | uv 0.12.5 |\n| Q2 | scikit-learn 1.7.2 |\n| Q3 | 0.533 |\n| Q4 | 0.77 |\n| Q5 | `python:3.11.15-slim-bookworm` |\n| Q6 | 0.77 |\n\nSave the notebook in Jupyter (Ctrl+S) to keep the new cells and outputs. Running the whole notebook from the top with Restart & Run All is also worth doing, so all the outputs come from one clean run.",
      "id": "c03e638e-2420-468d-82ea-29cc8c185643",
